    {
      "evidence_id": "e-3554d6af136381412c36",
      "text": "The capital of the island is the village of Kimolos, which hosts the majority of the island’s inhabitants. Smaller settlements that are inhabited mainly in the summer, while in the winter they have few inhabitants, are Psathi (port), Goupa, Kara, Prasa, Aliki, Bonatsa and Deka. The port and main port is Psathi, at the south-eastern end of the island and it is about 0.8 kilometers from Chorio. It has approximately 600 permanent residents, most of whom currently live in the Village.",
