    {
      "evidence_id": "e-54f5ae98559fe7f90a12",
      "text": "A beachside taverna at Kimolos port\nRawf8\nAs the sun dips and the island slowly stirs from its afternoon slumber, it’s time to head back into Chorio, which lies 4.5 kilometres northeast of Espera. Taxis here are infrequent and sometimes costly, so the best way to get around the island is to rent a car, scooter or ATV when you arrive in Psathi, the island’s only port village. Park outside Chorio’s pedestrianised boundary and stroll the chalk-lined maze of cobbled paths and whitewashed houses, popping into boutiques for handmade jewellery, ceramics and homeware, marvelling at the 15th-century kastro (castle), or exploring the blue-domed Church of Panagia Odigitria, which dates back to the 19th century.",
